course: dictionary
lesson: 1710
title: Cinema: a place, a trip, an art
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cinema is a building where people sit in rows and watch films on a big screen. «At the cinema you keep your feet on the floor and do not kick the seat in front.» The rule tells you that a cinema has seats, and that people sit still and quietly while the film plays.
explain: Use the words around cinema to check its meaning. «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint» tells you that a cinema is dark inside. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A building, a room, or a place with a screen. Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it.
explain: Cinema can also mean going to see a film, as in «go to the cinema» or «at the cinema». It can also mean the art of making films. Watch the words around it: the sentence tells you which meaning is used.
fact: A cinema is a building where people watch films on a big screen.
fact: «Go to the cinema» can mean going to see a film with friends or family.
fact: Cinema is also the art of making films.
fact: The plural of cinema is cinemas, as in «two cinemas in our town».
fact: «Parents decide what children watch at home, and cinemas must follow the age rules.» In UK cinemas, a 15 film may not be seen by anyone under 15.
exercise: «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint.» What is a cinema? | *A building where people watch films on a big screen | A bright place outdoors with sunshine | A shop that sells popcorn only | A kind of car
exercise: Ella says, «Let's go to the cinema at seven.» What does going to the cinema mean? | *Going to see a film | Going to sleep early | Going to the library to read | Going to buy a bicycle
exercise: Find the word in «In UK cinemas a 12A film may be seen by under-12s only with an adult» that names the places where films are shown. | 12A | *cinemas | adult | film
test: In a UK cinema, who may watch a 15 film? | *Nobody under 15 | Anyone, if their parents say yes | Only adults with a ticket | Only children under 12
test: Which is the plural of cinema? | cinema | cinemae | *cinemas | cinemaa
exam: Mia says, «I want to study the cinema because I love making films.» What does cinema mean here? | Ticket prices at the box office | *The art of making films | A building with a big screen | A kind of camera
